  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is inscribed in a semicircle whose diameter is \\(\\overline{AB},\\) then \\(\\overline{AC}+\\overline{BC}\\) must be:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "Equal to \\(\\overline{AB}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "Equal to \\(\\overline{AB}\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\ge \\overline{AB}\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\le \\overline{AB}\\sqrt2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\overline{AB}^{\\,2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p32.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By Thales’ theorem, \\(AC\\) and \\(BC\\) are the legs of a right triangle with hypotenuse \\(AB.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} (AC+BC)^2 &\\le2(AC^2+BC^2)\\\\ &=2AB^2. \\end{aligned} \\] Taking positive square roots gives \\(AC+BC\\le AB\\sqrt2,\\) with equality for an isosceles right triangle.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "The angle subtending the diameter is a right angle",
        "For legs \\(a,b\\), compare \\((a+b)^2\\) with \\(2(a^2+b^2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
